{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Observation\nOn the production MCP host, 2026-11-01 21:03-21:35 PST, one compaction sweep (`op=compact-sweep`) held the store write lock for 160-250 s per fold while folding 10 tickets (journald evidence on `radiant-benighted-warbler` and `overweak-deviant-shelduck`). The build included `f3cb9223d8c` (bug `graspable-fabled-skylark`), which moved the authorship history walks out of the lock.\nA canonical write waits at most about 181 s (30 s x 2 attempts x 3 passes). A writer that arrives just after a fold takes the lock gets only one pass before the fold ends, so a fold that holds the lock longer than that fails the write. The between-ticket handover fix in `radiant-benighted-warbler` does not shorten a single fold.\n\n## Measured (clone of `tickets` at `daa3a65239b^`, replaying the 10 production folds)\n- The first fold held the lock 58.1 s cold and 11.8-14.4 s warm; 92-98% of that was `identity.resolve_current_identity`, which with no identity pointer reduces every ticket in the store. Later folds held 0.5-2.7 s, mostly `git add` + `git commit`.\n- `identify_signer` -> `rebar.show_ticket` -> `ensure_fresh` fetched under the fold's lock, then `sync.reconverge` asked for the lock the fold already held (bug `congruent-demurrable-insect`).\n- The clone does NOT reproduce production's 160-250 s: folds that replay in under 1 s here held 220-243 s there. The production phase is unidentified, and the sweep worker's log was empty, so no production per-phase timing exists.\n\n## Scope of change 3269\n1. Resolve event attribution and each signed event's verifying key BEFORE the store write lock, following `finalize_event` (attribution before `write_and_push`) and `preresolve_unmapped_positions`.\n2. Run the locked body under `local_read_context`, so the fold never fetches and never re-requests its own lock.\n3. Log one WARNING line per fold naming the seconds spent in each phase: `attribution`, `signers`, `lock_wait`, `recover`, `parse`, `reduce`, `ledger`, `build_snapshot`, `write_retire`, `commit`, `held`.\n4. Install the stderr handler in the detached sweep worker, so its log (`compact-worker.log`) receives that line.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Identity attribution and signer lookups run before the store write lock; a test observes the lock dir at each `_match_by_email` and `identify_signer` call and sees none under the lock.\n- [ ] While the fold holds the lock it runs no `git fetch`, no `sync.reconverge`, and no second `lock.acquire`; a test with a remote and an expired freshness throttle checks each.\n- [ ] The snapshot's `author_id`/`author_email` and the authorship ledger are unchanged by pre-resolution; tests compare them.\n- [ ] Each fold logs exactly one WARNING timing line naming all 11 phases, including folds that skip inside the lock, and the detached sweep worker writes it to its log; tests check each.\n- [ ] Replaying the 10 production folds on the clone copy holds the store write lock under the writer's 60 s single-pass budget; the measurement is recorded in a ticket comment.\n- [ ] The production hold is diagnosed from the new timing lines: after the next production sweep, read `compact-worker.log` and record which phase consumed the 160-250 s per fold, in a ticket comment."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793719869092058001,"uuid":"2c8d9093-74ea-455b-b513-1f8223a7e320"}